## 8. Challenges and How I Solved Them

**Challenge 1 — Password validation feedback**  
I wanted to show specific messages for each rule rather than one generic "invalid password" message. I solved this by checking each rule in order and breaking out of the chain as soon as one fails, so the user gets one clear instruction at a time.

**Challenge 2 — Modal accessibility**  
Clicking outside the modal to close it required checking if the click target was the overlay itself (`e.target === modal`) rather than any child element inside it. This was a small but important UX detail.

**Challenge 3 — HTML attribute bug**  
During development the email and password inputs were rendering on the same row. This turned out to be a missing closing quote on the `autocomplete` attribute — `autocomplete="email required/>` instead of `autocomplete="email" required />`. A single typo was breaking the entire form layout, which was a good reminder to always validate HTML structure.

